WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.275
(upbeat music)

00:00:01.275 --> 00:00:03.505
- [Narrator] Celebrities
love endorsing presidents,

00:00:03.505 --> 00:00:06.020
and presidents love
celebrity endorsements.

00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:09.268
And this is the story of the
president that started it all.

00:00:09.268 --> 00:00:12.268
(upbeat jazz music)

00:00:13.753 --> 00:00:16.745
Warren Harding was the 29th
President of the United States.

00:00:16.745 --> 00:00:19.012
Before that, Harding was
a pretty generic Senator.

00:00:19.012 --> 00:00:22.005
The New York Times even dubbed
him "Faint and Colorless."

00:00:22.005 --> 00:00:24.500
So how the hell did he win the presidency?

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:27.504
Three words, Florence Kling Harding,

00:00:27.504 --> 00:00:29.509
his wife and true campaigner.

00:00:29.509 --> 00:00:31.522
Florence had her ear to the ground.

00:00:31.522 --> 00:00:34.278
Any time a famous or
influential person came to town,

00:00:34.278 --> 00:00:37.015
she would have them pose for
a photo on their front porch.

00:00:37.015 --> 00:00:39.763
So basically, the first political selfie.

00:00:39.763 --> 00:00:41.511
Enter Al Jolson:

00:00:41.511 --> 00:00:43.775
at the time deemed the
world's greatest entertainer.

00:00:43.775 --> 00:00:46.259
(bell dings)

00:00:46.259 --> 00:00:47.838
He sang, he danced,

00:00:47.838 --> 00:00:50.519
he even landed the first
talking role in a movie.

00:00:50.519 --> 00:00:51.485
Most importantly,

00:00:51.485 --> 00:00:52.754
he became the first celebrity

00:00:52.754 --> 00:00:55.518
to ever endorse a presidential candidate.

00:00:55.518 --> 00:00:58.017
Harding had several other
celebrity endorsements;

00:00:58.017 --> 00:01:00.518
most notably, Thomas
Edison and Henry Ford.

00:01:00.518 --> 00:01:01.523
And guess what?

00:01:01.523 --> 00:01:02.356
It worked.

00:01:03.251 --> 00:01:05.492
Warren Harding became our 29th President.

00:01:05.492 --> 00:01:06.325
And despite going down

00:01:06.325 --> 00:01:08.497
as one of the worst
presidents in U.S. history,

00:01:08.497 --> 00:01:11.268
his political selfies changed
the landscape forever.

00:01:11.268 --> 00:01:15.435
(U.S. Presidential
Anthem: Hail to the Chief)

